{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedReverseRow","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedReverseRow","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedInsertion"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowUninsert_sorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowUninsert_sorted","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseRow.lean#L182-L220","doc":"Reverse insertion keeps the row weakly increasing.\n\nThe replaced entry is the rightmost one strictly below `y`, so everything after it is already\n`≥ y`; and everything before it is `≤` the old entry, which is `< y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.exists_lt_of_rowUninsert_some","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.exists_lt_of_rowUninsert_some","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseRow.lean#L165-L180","doc":"`some` means some entry was strictly below `y` — there was something to replace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.forall_le_of_rowUninsert_none","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.forall_le_of_rowUninsert_none","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseRow.lean#L147-L163","doc":"`none` means every entry was at least `y` — the converse of `rowUninsert_of_forall_le`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.mem_rowUninsert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.mem_rowUninsert","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseRow.lean#L123-L145","doc":"Every entry of a reverse-inserted row is an old entry or the value `y` put in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowUninsert_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowUninsert_length","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseRow.lean#L108-L121","doc":"Reverse insertion never changes the row length. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowUninsert_rowInsert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowUninsert_rowInsert","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseRow.lean#L83-L106","doc":"**The inversion law.** If inserting `x` into a weakly-increasing row `r` bumps `y`, then\nreverse-inserting `y` into the resulting row recovers `r` and reports the inserted `x`.\n\n`rowInsert` and `rowUninsert` are therefore mutually inverse on the bumping branch, which is the\nbranch the RSK cascade runs on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowUninsert_of_forall_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowUninsert_of_forall_le","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseRow.lean#L70-L81","doc":"**Nothing to undo.** If every entry of `r` is at least `y`, reverse insertion leaves `r` alone\nand reports `none`. This is what makes the inversion law's base case go through: past the\ninsertion point a Schensted row is entirely `≥` the bumped value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowUninsert_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowUninsert_cons","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseRow.lean#L64-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowUninsert_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowUninsert_nil","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseRow.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowUninsert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowUninsert","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseRow.lean#L48-L60","doc":"**Reverse row insertion.** Undo a bump: replace the rightmost entry of `r` strictly less than\n`y` by `y`, returning `(newRow, some removed)`. If every entry is `≥ y` there is nothing to undo,\nand the row is returned unchanged with `none`.\n\nThe recursion descends to the end of the list first, so the *rightmost* eligible entry is the one\nreplaced — the mirror of `rowInsert`, which stops at the *leftmost* entry strictly greater than\nthe inserted value. ","signatureChunk":0}]}